<!-- Adaptive-icon monochrome layer: the same chip, in one colour, for themed icons.

     GEOMETRY AND SCALE MUST STAY IDENTICAL TO ic_launcher_foreground.xml. The two
     layers are the adaptive icon's foreground and its themed twin, and a mask that
     changes shape between them is a launcher that redraws the icon when a theme is
     applied. Only the colours differ, and only because a monochrome layer states the
     shape and lets the system tint it.

     The inserts and the accent ring are dropped rather than drawn as holes: at the size
     a themed icon renders, an 8-spoke break on a 24-unit grid fills in and the chip
     reads as a blob. The rim and the field keep the silhouette, which is what the tint
     is there to carry.

     The plate is absent on purpose. This layer is composited over the background's own
     colour, and a plate here would be a second background. -->
